is_author":false,"tags":["reversing","windows"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/jwidjn","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/jwidjn/inside_windows_i_o_manager_deep_dive_into"},{"short_id":"jxhi2i","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:29:11.053-05:00","title":"A sustainable web career, for when all this blows over","url":"https://dbushell.com/2026/10/07/sustainable-web-career/","score":38,"flags":1,"comment_count":23,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"nrvous","user_is_author":false,"tags":["vibecoding","web"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/jxhi2i","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/jxhi2i/sustainable_web_career_for_when_all_this"},{"short_id":"tcmpcw","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:16.404-05:00","title":"Pared - remove unwanted Apple Intelligence models without disabling SIP","url":"https://github.com/4evy/pared","score":14,"flags":1,"comment_count":3,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"FlameFlag","user_is_author":true,"tags":["mac","show","vibecoding"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/tcmpcw","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/tcmpcw/pared_remove_unwanted_apple"},{"short_id":"uvpts7","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:11:34.419-05:00","title":"Perseus: A Fail-Slow Detection Framework for Cloud Storage Systems (2023)","url":"https://www.usenix.org/system/files/fast23-lu.pdf","score":1,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"\u003cp\u003eAbstract: The newly-emerging “fail-slow” failures plague both software and hardware where the victim components are still functioning yet with degraded performance. To address this problem, this paper presents PERSEUS, a practical fail-slow detection framework for storage devices. PERSEUS leverages a light regression-based model to fast pinpoint and analyze fail-slow failures at the granularity of drives. Within a 10-month close monitoring on 248K drives, PERSEUS managed to find 304 fail-slow cases. Isolating them can reduce the (node-level) 99.99th tail latency by 48%. We assemble a large-scale fail-slow dataset (including 41K normal drives and 315 verified fail-slow drives) from our production traces, based on which we provide root cause analysis on fail-slow drives covering a variety of ill-implemented scheduling, hardware defects, and environmental factors. We have released the dataset to the public for fail-slow study.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Abstract: The newly-emerging “fail-slow” failures plague both software and hardware where the victim components are still functioning yet with degraded performance. To address this problem, this paper presents PERSEUS, a practical fail-slow detection framework for storage devices. PERSEUS leverages a light regression-based model to fast pinpoint and analyze fail-slow failures at the granularity of drives. Within a 10-month close monitoring on 248K drives, PERSEUS managed to find 304 fail-slow cases. Isolating them can reduce the (node-level) 99.99th tail latency by 48%. We assemble a large-scale fail-slow dataset (including 41K normal drives and 315 verified fail-slow drives) from our production traces, based on which we provide root cause analysis on fail-slow drives covering a variety of ill-implemented scheduling, hardware defects, and environmental factors. We have released the dataset to the public for fail-slow study.","submitter_user":"typesanitizer","user_is_author":false,"tags":["distributed","pdf","performance"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/uvpts7","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/uvpts7/perseus_fail_slow_detection_framework"},{"short_id":"0xpi8s","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:03:04.730-05:00","title":"Why We Should Inject Dependencies","url":"https://gist.github.com/alassek/1a185a8cdae20ddd991a8cd3cd90d347","score":7,"flags":0,"comment_count":7,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"PuercoPop","user_is_author":false,"tags":["ruby"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/0xpi8s","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/0xpi8s/why_we_should_inject_dependencies"}]